Z||000000||ponya||02-15-2001||09:48 PM||||I was shopping around tonight when of course I wound up in the automotive section of the store. I saw a set of seat covers made by Allison. They were called Euro covers and looked really nice for a temporary fix. I took one out of its package and measured it. It should fit a stock seat with no problem. Anyone heard of these covers? I'd like to check before I buy a set and find out they are junk. Any imput appreciated. thanks,  Bob||||reg||5
Z||000001||CozmoPooky||02-16-2001||01:38 PM||||I got a set of them last week as a "temporary" fix until I do Mr. Mike's real leathers.  They match the grey color of my interior quite well but don't fit around the headrest part very good (I may finesse them this weekend).  They also add about 1" to the seat thickness, so you'll be closer to the roof and steering wheel (I'm 6'3'', so it took some getting used to).  All things considered, a good deal since they were on sale ($30-Kmart) and look MUCH better than my weasel-ripped stock covers.<P>------------------<BR>Cozmo<BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>'87 Duke Coupe     <BR>'85 2M6 Targa<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bothfierossig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
